  "Main topic of the publication": "This study investigates the role of aberrant DNA methylation and gene expression of imprinted genes in the placenta in relation to intrauterine growth restriction (IUGR). The study identifies that DNA methylation is less stable at placenta-specific imprinted differentially methylated regions (DMRs) compared to ubiquitous DMRs, and IUGR-associated expression differences were identified for several imprinted transcripts independent of allelic methylation.",
